+- **A merge is verified before a gate starts (experiment; card 374 retro, Decider D243).** While this entry is on trial: before the facilitator's baseline gate, a reviewer's replay or a sign-off clone starts, the card's gate record names the tested commit as `git rev-parse HEAD` of the checkout under test and shows that it contains the commit under test (`git merge-base --is-ancestor <commit> HEAD` with its exit status, or `git branch --contains <commit>`); a `git merge --ff-only` is followed by a check of its own exit status and of the resulting HEAD (its output is never reduced to its last line, which hid a refusal); a gate run on a tree that does not contain the commit under test is stopped and discarded, and the gate record says so; the facilitator runs the two commands by hand until a gate-start script prints them (the script and its planted-fail test, a merge refused because main moved, are written red first as a tooling card filed with this pick).
+  - Hypothesis: printing the tested HEAD and its ancestry before a gate stops a gate from running on a tree without the commit under test. Metric: gate runs started on a tree that did not contain the commit under test per card (card 374: 1, about 3 minutes lost, caught by chance when a review prompt showed the old commit), target 0. Counter-metric: seconds added per gate start. Trial: the next 3 cards, counted from Decider D243. Owner: the facilitator.
